 - 2026-06-17: PHASE A1 (HEADLINE; SETTLE the in-generation moat) -- BUILD a DiNa-LRM-style LEAK-ROBUST partial-state reward scorer (arXiv:2602.11146 VERIFIED). .400 (exp4325) found the .399 in-generation moat did NOT replicate because the exp4292 partial-state scorer LEAKED on a 2nd corpus (scorer_leak_recheck_passed=false): it recovered answer-bearing cells from position cues rather than genuinely scoring the masked denoising state. ROOT-CAUSE FIX (DiNa-LRM, 2602.11146 'Beyond VLM-Based Rewards: Diffusion-Native Latent Reward Modeling'): a timestep-conditioned reward head trained DIRECTLY on noisy/masked DiffusionGemma canvases (noise-calibrated uncertainty, inference-time noise ensembling), NOT a post-hoc scorer that peeks at clean cells. HARD GATE: the scorer must stay ORACLE-DISTINCT UNDER ANSWER-CELL MASKING on >=2 oracle-distinct corpora -- with the answer cells masked, the reward signal must NOT recover the answer (collapses to chance on the masked-answer probe) AND must still rank partial states by genuine process quality. Emit scorer_leak_audit_passed BARE bool := (the scorer SURVIVES the masked-answer leak audit on BOTH corpora: no answer recovery + non-degenerate process ranking). Deliverable: the persisted scorer module + the leak-audit artifact. verifier_is_oracle=false. If NO leak-robust scorer can be built (it always leaks or always degenerates) -> scorer_leak_audit_passed=false + honest_verdict complete_no_leak_robust_partial_state_scorer (decision-grade: the partial-state-scoring direction is not viable, retire). NO TRM training; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: leak_robust_partial_state_scorer_built; results/experiment_4337_leak_robust_partial_state_scorer_build.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE A2 (HEADLINE; SETTLE the in-generation moat -> DiffusionGemma gate) -- GATED on exp4337 scorer_leak_audit_passed==true: RE-RUN the in-generation moat replication on the 2ND corpus with the LEAK-ROBUST scorer (exp4337). .400 (exp4325) failed to replicate because the OLD exp4292 scorer leaked on corpus-2; exp4337 rebuilds it leak-robust (DiNa-LRM, audited under answer-cell masking on >=2 corpora). This is the DEFINITIVE replication: EXACT exp4315 harness -- unguided + EntRGi engaged control (2602.05000) + self-reward SMC (2602.01849, the must-beat intrinsic baseline) + Carnot reward-guided step-stitching (2602.22871) using the leak-robust scorer; the no-op guard (controls_differentiated); an INDEPENDENT leak re-check on the leak-robust scorer ON THE 2ND CORPUS -- at n>=80/arm, >=3 seeds for power. Emit in_generation_moat_replicates BARE bool := (Carnot-stitched - best-engaged-control > 0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND controls_differentiated AND Carnot-stitched - self-reward-SMC > 0) ON THE 2ND CORPUS with the LEAK-ROBUST scorer. verifier_is_oracle=false. This DECIDES the DiffusionGemma gate: a replication FLIPS it (the moat is real, leak-robust, headline-grade); a powered failure-to-replicate even WITH a leak-robust scorer RETIRES the in-generation moat as corpus-specific (retire_if_same_verdict: true). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: in_generation_moat_replicates; results/experiment_4338_in_generation_moat_replicate_leak_robust.json
 - 2026-06-17: PHASE B1 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY 2026-06-17) -- the FIRST E3 solve: ar25 -> L1 with EXPLORE-VERIFY-PLAN. .400 (exp4327) reached verifier_best_accuracy 0.89 on ar25 (the closest E3 has come) but offline_reproduced=false, plan_executed=false -- it PLANNED before it had verified the mechanics, and ar25 got only ONE refactor round (timed out under live codex contention). FIX (two VERIFIED SOTA methods): AERA explore-verify-plan (arXiv:2605.25931 -- separate EXPLORE/VERIFY/PLAN; the EXPLORE phase collects verifier-gated transition lemmas, PLAN only after the model passes mechanic checks) + Agent2World adaptive world-model testing (arXiv:2512.22336 -- adaptive unit tests surface the hidden-rule gap before planning). The codex agent IS the proposer (uses collect_transitions/WorldModelVerifier/load_engine/plan_and_execute as tools; WRITES results/arc_e3/ar25/world_model.py; NO nested CodexProposer). INCREMENTAL-PROGRESS scoped: +1 level (L1). HARD gate: offline_reproduced=true AND reproduced_levels>=1 (arc_solver_kit.reproduce). An honest partial (best verifier_accuracy + the residual mismatch CLASS as a missing-world-model-rule gap in ops/verifier_gaps.md) is PROGRESS. verifier_is_oracle=true (the SOLVE is EXECUTION-GROUNDED -- ARC north-star progress, NOT an oracle-distinct moat). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission; run when codex is NOT saturated; cap per-task wall-time. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success_e3_ar25_L1_reproduced; results/experiment_4339_e3_explore_verify_plan_ar25.json
